Since we only have eight drones in total, our best option to reduce overall damage is to keep Field_2’s four drones in place and “steal” one drone from the low‑threat Field_4 (dropping it to two drones, so that field goes from full to partial protection) and assign that drone to Field_3. That way, Field_3 becomes fully protected (with two drones) and Field_4’s potential damage is small (threat level 0.03), while Field_1 remains unprotected. This allocation minimizes expected overall damage.
